          "modelAnswer": "A neural network learns its own features. The input is just tokens mapped to embeddings, and the hidden layers (CNN filters, RNN states, attention…) compute intermediate representations. Because everything is differentiable, the gradient of the task loss trains these layers end to end, so they become detectors of whatever patterns are useful for the task (e.g. a CNN filter for 'not good'). The network replaces hand-designed features with learned ones; the human only chooses the architecture and data.",
