          "concept": "Multiple convolutional kernels",
          "type": "written",
          "marks": 2,
          "question": "Explain why it is necessary to have multiple convolutional kernels in a single layer of a CNN. (2 Marks)",
          "modelAnswer": "Each kernel (filter) is a single pattern detector: it learns to respond to one kind of local pattern, e.g. one n-gram feature such as 'not good'. Text contains many different useful patterns, so a layer needs many kernels (each producing its own feature map) to capture them all, often with different widths for different n-gram lengths.",
