          "question": "Explain the purpose of residual connections and layer normalisation in the Transformer. (4 Marks)",
          "modelAnswer": "Residual connections: each sublayer's output is added to its input, x + F(x). The block only has to learn an update (and can learn to do nothing), gradients flow directly through the skip path, and the loss landscape becomes much smoother, which makes deep stacks trainable (the idea comes from ResNet).\nLayer normalisation: after each residual addition, each token's vector is normalised over its features (mean 0, variance 1), then scaled and shifted by learned γ, β. This keeps activations at a stable scale as many blocks are stacked (stops values from exploding or drifting), which stabilises and speeds up training.",
