          "modelAnswer": "Catastrophic forgetting: when all of a pre-trained model's weights are fine-tuned on a new task, the updates can overwrite the general knowledge learned during pre-training, so the model loses abilities it had.\nAdapters and LoRA freeze the pre-trained weights and train only a small number of new parameters (adapters: small bottleneck layers inserted into each block; LoRA: a low-rank update BA added to the weights). The original knowledge stays intact, the per-task additions are small to store, and the frozen base can be shared across tasks.",
