          "type": "written",
          "marks": 4,
          "question": "Given a set of items $S = \\{1, 2, \\cdots, n\\}$ and $m$ proper subsets $S_j$ of $S$, $j = 1, 2, \\cdots, m$. You wants to covers all items in $S$ by choosing a number of $S_j$ with minimum cost; the cost of choosing $S_j$ is $c_j$. Write down the mathematical model of the weighted set covering problem by defining decision variables for optimization. Describe the physical meaning of the constraint sets in the mathematical model. [3+1 Marks ]",
          "modelAnswer": "Data: $a_{ij} = 1$ if item $i$ is in $S_j$, $a_{ij} = 0$ otherwise ($i = 1, \\dots, n$; $j = 1, \\dots, m$).\nDecision variables: $x_j = 1$ if subset $S_j$ is chosen, $x_j = 0$ otherwise.\n$$\\min \\sum_{j=1}^{m} c_j x_j$$\n$$\\text{s.t.}\\quad \\sum_{j=1}^{m} a_{ij} x_j \\ge 1, \\quad i = 1, \\dots, n$$\n$$x_j \\in \\{0, 1\\}, \\quad j = 1, \\dots, m$$\nMeaning: the objective is the total cost of the chosen subsets. The constraint for item $i$ says that at least one chosen subset contains item $i$, i.e. every item of $S$ is covered at least once. $x_j \\in \\{0, 1\\}$: each subset is either taken or not.",
