          "question": "Consider the following bi-partite graph\nfor which the costs $c_{ij}$ are given as\n$$c_{11} = 2, c_{12} = 3, c_{13} = 4,$$\n$$c_{21} = 3, c_{22} = 4, c_{23} = 1,$$\n$$c_{31} = 4, c_{32} = 2, c_{33} = 3.$$\nDefine the variables for the minimization problem and present your mathematical model. Define the meaning of each of your 6 constraints involved. [3 + 2 Marks ]",
          "modelAnswer": "Variables: $x_{ij} = 1$ if worker $i$ is assigned to job $j$, $x_{ij} = 0$ otherwise ($i, j \\in \\{1, 2, 3\\}$).\n$$\\min \\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\sum_{j=1}^{3} c_{ij}x_{ij} = 2x_{11} + 3x_{12} + 4x_{13} + 3x_{21} + 4x_{22} + x_{23} + 4x_{31} + 2x_{32} + 3x_{33}$$\nsubject to the 6 constraints\n$$x_{11} + x_{12} + x_{13} = 1,\\quad x_{21} + x_{22} + x_{23} = 1,\\quad x_{31} + x_{32} + x_{33} = 1$$\n$$x_{11} + x_{21} + x_{31} = 1,\\quad x_{12} + x_{22} + x_{32} = 1,\\quad x_{13} + x_{23} + x_{33} = 1$$\n$$x_{ij} \\in \\{0, 1\\}$$\nMeaning: the first three (one per worker, $\\sum_j x_{ij} = 1$) say each worker $i$ does exactly one job; the last three (one per job, $\\sum_i x_{ij} = 1$) say each job $j$ is done by exactly one worker.\n(Not asked, but useful: the optimum is $x_{11} = x_{23} = x_{32} = 1$ with cost $2 + 1 + 2 = 5$; checking all $3! = 6$ assignments gives 9, 5, 9, 8, 9, 12.)",
