          "modelAnswer": "Main objective of the Metropolis algorithm: to numerically generate sample points (a Markov chain of solutions) from a probability distribution that cannot be sampled directly, here the Boltzmann (equilibrium / stationary) distribution at temperature $T$. In SA it is the rule that decides whether a trial solution replaces the current one: better solutions are always accepted and worse ones are accepted with a probability that shrinks as $T$ is lowered, so the search can climb out of local minima early on and settles near a good minimum as $T \\to 0$.\nMetropolis acceptance probability (minimisation) of moving from the current solution $(x, E_x)$ to the trial solution $(y, E_y)$ at temperature $T_t$:\n$$A_{xy}(T_t) = \\min\\left\\{1,\\ \\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{E_y - E_x}{T_t}\\right)\\right\\}.$$\nIf $E_y \\le E_x$ the exponent is $\\ge 0$, so $A_{xy} = 1$ and $y$ is always accepted. If $E_y > E_x$, $y$ is accepted when a uniform random number $r \\in (0,1)$ satisfies $r < \\exp(-(E_y - E_x)/T_t)$.",
          "rubric": [
            {
              "point": "Generates sample points from a distribution that cannot be sampled directly (the equilibrium/Boltzmann distribution at temperature $T$)",
              "marks": 2
            },
            {
              "point": "In SA: accepts all improvements and some worse moves, so it can escape local minima",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "point": "$A_{xy}(T) = \\min\\{1, \\exp(-(E_y - E_x)/T)\\}$",
              "marks": 1
            },
            {
              "point": "Use: always accept if $E_y \\le E_x$, else accept if a uniform $r < \\exp(-(E_y - E_x)/T)$",
              "marks": 1
            }
          ],
          "explanation": "Follows the handwritten solution in Past Paper Solutions 2024 Exam.pdf p. 8. Course notes: Metropolis rule and the SA algorithm, DisCopt.pdf PDF p. 51 (eq. 101, \"accept if exp(−(f(y) − f(x))/T) > random(0,1)\"); sa.pdf (lecturer's SA pseudocode, same test).",
          "variantOf": "do-metropolis"
