          "modelAnswer": "Both split the vertex set $V$ of a weighted graph into two disjoint parts and are judged by the total weight of the edges that run between the two parts (in the course notes both maximise it).\nGraph bisection: the two parts must have the same number of vertices, $|V_1| = |V_2| = n/2$ ($n$ even). In the model $x_i \\in \\{1, -1\\}$ this is the extra constraint $\\sum_i x_i = 0$.\nMax-2-cut (max-cut): the two parts $S$ and $V \\setminus S$ can have any sizes; there is no balance constraint.\nSo the main difference is the equal-size (balance) constraint of bisection.",
