          "question": "In the context of Branch and Bound algorithm for a minimization problem answer the following questions: [2 + 3 Marks ]\n(ii) Give three cases when a subproblem (or node in the tree) is deleted (not considered for further investigation).",
          "modelAnswer": "For a minimisation problem, with the best feasible (incumbent) value as the upper bound $u$ and the relaxed value $l(S_i)$ of a subproblem as its lower bound, a subproblem is deleted (fathomed) when:\n1. Bound: $l(S_i) \\ge u$ (in the notes $l(S_i) > u(S)$): even its relaxation cannot beat the best solution already found, so no solution in that branch can be better.\n2. Integer solution: the relaxed solution of the subproblem is already integer feasible. It is the best solution in that branch, so the incumbent and upper bound are updated if it is better, and there is nothing left to branch on.\n3. Infeasible: the relaxed subproblem has no feasible solution, so the branch contains no solutions at all.",
