          "marks": 6,
          "question": "Suppose GA is used to solve binary optimization problem. Tournament selection is used to select two parents solutions $x_1 = 10101$ and $x_2 = 01110$ for reproduction. Describe the tournament selection process in brief. Obtain two new solutions ($y_1$ and $y_2$) using a double point crossover with the integers $n_1$=2 and $n_2$=4. [2 + 4 Marks ]",
          "modelAnswer": "Tournament selection: pick two members of the current population at random (different indices) and compare their fitness; the fitter one becomes parent A. Repeat with another random pair to get parent B (members may be picked again). Fitter solutions win more tournaments, so they reproduce more often, but weak ones still have a chance.\nConvention: the lecturer's GA pseudocode (DiscreteGAcode.pdf p. 2) swaps the genes in positions $n_1, n_1 + 1, \\dots, n_2$ inclusive between the two parents.\nPositions:   1 | 2 3 4 | 5\n$x_1$ = 1 | 0 1 0 | 1\n$x_2$ = 0 | 1 1 1 | 0\nSwap the genes in positions 2–4 (\"010\" and \"111\"), keep positions 1 and 5:\n$y_1$ = 1 | 1 1 1 | 1 = $11111$\n$y_2$ = 0 | 0 1 0 | 0 = $00100$\n(If instead the cuts are placed after gene 2 and after gene 4, only positions 3–4 are swapped, giving $y_1 = 10111$ and $y_2 = 01100$. State the convention you use.)",
