          "question": "You are given a set of data $\\{(y^1, x^1), (y^2, x^2), \\cdots, (y^N, x^N)\\}$, $N >> 4$. Assume that the response variable, $y$, relates to the predictors, $x = (x_1, x_2)^T$, through some unknown function expressed generally as: $y = f(x) + \\epsilon$, $\\epsilon \\sim N(0, \\sigma)$, $\\epsilon$ is unrelated to $x$. Use the estimator, $\\hat{f}(x)$, of $f(x)$ as\n$$\\hat{f}(x) = \\beta_o + \\beta_1 x_1 + \\beta_2 x_2 + \\beta_3 x_1 x_2$$\nand answer the following questions:\n(iii) Identify the normal equation in the solution process of (2). [5 + 5 + 2 Marks ]",
